  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 310 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nFriday Evening onward...Convective coverage should be diurnally\nwaning into the midday. Boundary placement should make for high\ntemperature variance from north to south. Timing the next \nridge-riding short wave will be likely late day into the \nevening. The convective mode and coverage for Friday night is\nhighly uncertain, with some CAM signal of a forward-propagating\nMCS, which would bring at least a scattered damaging wind \nthreat. Regardless of mode, heavy rain to a water sensitive CWA\nresulted in us extending the Flood Watch.\n\nSaturday through Wednesday...Latest ensemble and upper jet trends \nsuggest the upper ridge and heat dome to get pressed eastward \ntemporarily maintaining the ring of fire for the weekend with the local \narea precariously near the periphery through at least Sunday. \nStorm chances will continue as well with high dew point air, \nbut then some signs early next week of upper ridge retrogrades, \nallowing for more of a northwest flow push down the upper\nMississippi River Valley. A resultant drier and cooler Monday \nwould be much welcome by then.",
